data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Good. The package has styles at dist/styles/*.css. The developer brief mentions styles/components/app-shell.css and styles/components/button.css, but those don't exist as separate directories - they're in dist/styles/components/*.css. However, the package exports say `\"./styles/*.css\": \"./dist/styles/*.css\"`, so importing `@codesweep-ai/ui/styles/core.css` resolves to dist/styles/core.css. And `@codesweep-ai/ui/styles/components/app-shell.css` resolves to dist/styles/components/app-shell.css. Good, so the developer brief paths are correct via the export map.\n\nNow, the package version is 0.3.0. The catalog says components like AppShell, Button. The d.ts confirms AppShell exports Header, Footer, AppShell.\n\nLet me design the interface. I need to write DESIGN.md. I should keep it simple and clear. The developer brief says to use React with Vite, useState, install @codesweep-ai/ui, use AppShell with Header/Footer, Button, and colour tokens.\n\nDesign choices:\n- App title in header: \"Hello\"\n- Footer: \"Built with @codesweep-ai/ui\"\n- Main content: a large greeting \"Hello, world!\" centered\n- Four buttons below to change greeting colour: Teal, Amber, Rose, Sky\n- Use tokens: --color-cat-2 (teal), --color-cat-3 (amber), --color-cat-4 (rose), --color-cat-9 (sky)\n- Layout: full viewport, centered content, buttons in a row\n\nActually, the design should probably use specific tokens. Let me also think about whether to use Page component. The mission says Header, Footer, Button, and colour tokens come from the package. It doesn't require Page but I can use it for layout. Actually, the AppShell provides the header/footer chrome, and the content area is scrollable. The Page component is for page-level content container. I think using AppShell + Page would be clean.\n\nBut the mission says \"four things come from it: a Header, a Footer, its Button for the colour buttons, and its colour tokens for the greeting colours.\" So we need exactly Header, Footer, Button, and colour tokens from the package. Page is extra but fine.\n\nLet me write the DESIGN.md. I should also think about the Vite config. React app with Vite. Need package.json, vite.config.js, index.html, src/main.jsx, src/App.jsx, etc.\n\nActually, the orchestrator only writes DESIGN.md. The developer implements everything. So I should keep DESIGN.md focused on design decisions and high-level structure, not implementation details, though I can mention the required imports and structure to ensure they use the design system correctly.\n\nLet me create DESIGN.md now."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789849004,"id":"chatcmpl-490f88613293438a90acd15c3b4f3d29","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

